<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIAN PROTESTERS STORM PARLIAMENT.</title>
<headline>BULGARIAN PROTESTERS STORM PARLIAMENT.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian anti-government protesters stormed doors of parliament on Friday after breaking riot police cordon to demand early parliamentary elections for the first time in modern Bulgarian history.</p>
<p>Opposition supporters surrounded parliament by a human chain in a day-long protest after the ruling Bulgarian Socialist Party rejected to vote on a &quot;salvation declaration&quot; which demanded early parliamentary elections, eyewitness said.</p>
</text>
